                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion+of+smooth+manifolds"} immersion
              %li
                %p
                  the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
            %p
              A
              %em closed embedding
              is an embedding such that the image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(X) \subset Y
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
          %h3#SyntheticDefinitionInDifferentialCohesion Synthetic definition in differential cohesion
          %p
            The classical definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldsEmbedding"}
            of
            %em embedding
            of smooth manifolds should have the following axiomatization in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} differentially cohesive infinity-topos theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modalities"} adjoint modalities
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℜ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊣
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℑ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊣
                        %mtd
                          %mi &amp;
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ∨
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ∨
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ʃ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊣
                        %mtd
                          %mo ♭
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊣
                        %mtd
                          %mo ♯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \Re &amp;\dashv&amp; \Im &amp;\dashv&amp; \&amp;
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \vee &amp;&amp; \vee
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; &amp;#643; &amp;\dashv&amp;  \flat &amp;\dashv&amp; \sharp
                  }
          %p Of these we now use
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
          %p
            Then given a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi i
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \overset{i}{\longrightarrow} X
            we have
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                being a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                means that it is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism in an (infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                being an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersion
                means (by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "immersion+of+smooth+manifolds#InDifferentialCohesion"} this Discussion
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+unramified+morphism"} formally unramified morphism
                in that the comparison morphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℑ
                          %mi X
                      %mi ℑ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      U \longrightarrow X \times_{\Im X} \Im(U)
              %p
                into the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                along the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
                is a monomorphism;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                being an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
                means (by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "subspace+topology#UniversalProperty"} this Discussion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mo ♯
                          %mi X
                      %mo ♯
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      U \longrightarrow X \times_{\sharp X} \sharp U
              %p
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            this should mean that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi_U \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Type
          %p
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                it factors through the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+of+propositions"} universe of propositions
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Prop
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prop
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert -\vert_{-1}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+types"} modal types
                (where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert-\vert_{-1}
                is the
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncation+modality"} (-1)-truncation modality
            %li
              %p
                it factors through the universe of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
                = succeed ";" do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    submodal types
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/submodal+types"} ?
            %li
              %p
                it factors through the universe of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+types"} modal types
          %h2#Examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#nonexample Nonexample
            %p
              %strong (immersions that are not embeddings)
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/Immersion.png", :width => "150"}/
            %p
              Consider an immersion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; (a,b) \to \mathbb{R}^2
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+interval"} open interval
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+plane"} Euclidean plane
              (or the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding of smooth manifolds
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              of open subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
              do not exhaust the open subsets of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
            %div{:style => "float:left;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/Figure8Immersion.png", :width => "400"}/
            %p
              As a concrete examples, consider the function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi sin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi π
                      %mo ,
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (sin(2-), sin(-)) \;\colon\; (-\pi, \pi) \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^2
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective"} injective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mo ±
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = \pm \pi
              “touching” the point at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 0
            %blockquote
              %p
                graphics grabbed from
                %a{:href => "https://books.google.de/books?id=xygVcKGPsNwC=PP1=PA86=y#v=onepage=false"} Lee
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          #ProperInjectiveImmersionsAreEquivalentlyTheClosedEmbeddings.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (proper injective immersions are equivalently the closed embeddings)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersion
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a closed embedding (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldsEmbedding"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since topological manifolds are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "locally+compact+topological+space#TopologicalManifoldsAreLocallyCompact"}> this example
              ), this follows directly since
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "embedding+of+topological+spaces#InjectiveProperMapsAreEquivalentlyTheClosedEmbeddings"} injective proper maps into locally compact spaces are equivalently closed embeddings
          %p
          #ExistenceOfSiceCharts.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (submanifolds admit slice charts)
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \colon \Sigma \hookrightarrow X
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
              = succeed ":" do
                %em slice charts
            %p
              For each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in \Sigma
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \supset U \xrightarrow{\phi} \mathbb{R}^n
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in U \subset M
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(\Sigma \cap U)
              is a rectilinear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperplane"} hyperplane
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(U) \subset \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lee12"} Lee 2012, Thm. 5.8
          %p hupf
          %h3#EmbeddingIntoEuclideanSpace Embedding into Euclidean space
          %p
            Every smooth manifold has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding of smooth manifolds
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^k
            of some dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            For
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            smooth manifolds this is easy to see (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactManifoldEmbedsIntoLargeDimensionalEuclideanSpace"}
            below), while the generalization to non-compact smooth manifolds requires a tad more work (theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#theorema"}
            below). What is non-trivial is to find the minimum dimension of the ambient Euclidean space for which embedding in general still exist. The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+embedding+theorem"} Whitney embedding theorem
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WhitneyStrongEmbeddingTheorem"}
            below) says that this is twice the dimension of the manifolds to be embedded.
          #CompactManifoldEmbedsIntoLargeDimensionalEuclideanSpace.num_example
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has an embedding (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldsEmbedding"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              of dimension
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mtext embd
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \overset{\text{embd}}{\hookrightarrow} \mathbb{R}^k
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{\mathbb{R}^n \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi_i}{\longrightarrow} U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
            %p
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              exhibiting the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset I
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{\mathbb{R}^n \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi_i}{\to} U_i \subset X\}_{i \in J \subset I}
            %p is still an open cover.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i \in C^\infty(X,\mathbb{R})\}_{i \in J }
              subordinate to this cover with
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
              (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "partition+of+unity#SmoothManifoldAdmitsSmoothPartitionsOfUnity"} this prop.
            %p
              This we may use to extend the inverse
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} chart
              identifications
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \supset \;\; U_i \underoverset{\simeq}{\psi_i}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p to smooth functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat \psi_i \;\colon\; X \to \mathbb{R}^{n}
            %p by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi ψ
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mi i
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mtext otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat \psi_i
                    \\;\colon\;
                    x
                    \\mapsto
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    f_i(x) \cdot \psi_i(x) &amp;\vert&amp; x \in U_i \subset X
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
            %p The idea now is to combine all these functions to obtain an injective function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\hat \psi_i)_{i \in J}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X \longrightarrow (\mathbb{R}^n)^{\vert J\vert }
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n \cdot {\vert J \vert }}
                    \\,.
            %p
              But while this is injective, it need not be an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives"} derivatives
              of the product functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i \cdot \psi_i
              may vanish, even though the derivatives of the two factors do not vanish separately. However this is readily fixed by adding yet more ambient coordinates and considering the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\hat \psi_i, f_i)_{i \in I}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\left(\mathbb{R}^{n+1}\right)^{\vert J \vert}
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\cdot {\vert J \vert}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is an immersion. Hence it remains to see that it is also an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "embedding+of+topological+spaces#OpenClosedContinuousInjectionsAreEmbeddings"} this prop
              it is sufficient to see that the injective continuous function is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              by assumption, and since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps+from+compact+spaces+to+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed+and+proper"} maps from compact spaces to Hausdorff spaces are closed and proper
          #ManifoldEmbedsIntoLargeDimensionalEuclideanSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (Hausdorff, sigma-compact), there exists some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has an embedding into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              of dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            What is harder to prove is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            may be chosen to be as small as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
          #WhitneyStrongEmbeddingTheorem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney%27s+strong+embedding+theorem"}> Whitney's strong embedding theorem
                )
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (Hausdorff, sigma-compact), there is an embedding into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              of dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
            %p
              In fact this bound is minimal, there are smooth manifolds of dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              which have no embedding into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^k
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt 2n
          %h2#space_of_embeddings Space of Embeddings
          %p
            This section follows from a discussion on the
            %em Algebraic Topology
            mailing list as to making concrete the contractibility of the space of embeddings of a smooth manifold in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} ^{(\infty )}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+spaces"} Euclidean spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          %p
            Showing that it is not empty is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
            argument. As the space that we are embedding in is infinite dimensional, we do not need to resort to either compactness or Whitney’s embedding theorem to obtain an embedding. One of these would be required if we wanted to show that our embedding was actually in some finite Euclidean space.
          %p
            The contraction depends on certain properties of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} ^{(\infty )}
            which are quite general and seemingly unrelated to the question of embeddings. The key property is the existence of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shift+map"} shift map
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sphere"} infinite sphere
          #sectionb.num_section
          %h3#existence_of_embeddings.num_section Existence of Embeddings
          #theorema.num_theorem.thplain
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be an infinite dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+topological+vector+space"} locally convex topological vector space
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldsEmbedding"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \hookrightarrow  V
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We shall start with the case
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{R} ^{(\infty )}
            %p
              As
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a smooth manifold, we can choose a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ \rho _{i} : i \in I\}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              with the property that for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ρ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho _{i}
